To run the code in Visual Studio Code, you can use the Command Palette or the keyboard shortcut `Ctrl + Shift + R`. In the Command Palette, type "Java: Run" to run the current file.

Here's an example of what the console output might look like:
```
2Sum.java
2Sum.java:4: error C2146: 'numbers' was not declared in this scope
         numbers (int)
```
This is because `numbers` is a variable defined within the method, but it's not accessible outside the method. To fix this, you can pass an array of integers as an argument to the `twoSum` method:
```java
// 2Sum.java

public class Solution {
    public int[] twoSum(int[] numbers, int target) {
        for (int i = 0; i < numbers.length; i++) {
            int complement = target - numbers[i];
            if (numbers.indexOf(complement) != -1) {
                return new int[] {i, numbers.indexOf(complement)};
            }
        }
        // If no solution is found
        return null;
    }
}
```
This code will find the pair of numbers that add up to the target sum.

